WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.300
Here she is, arriving from her new home in South Korea ...

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:05.220
Please welcome Eunsun Kim!

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:21.480
Welcome to London!

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.600
Thank you.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.700
And to a Scandinavian television show.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.660
It's very great to be here!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.360
You've told your story, actually, in your own book.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.080
Yes.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:35.680
And it's called «North Korea – Nine years escape from hell».

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.920
I wonder, as a kid growing up in North Korea ...

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.180
... what did you know about the world outside?

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:51.340
Actually, we didn't know much about the outside world. Yeah.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:59.420
Because when you're in North Korea, the North Korean government doesn't allow us to know about other countries.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:03.420
And the information from other countries cannot come into North Korea.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.780
They strongly control the ...

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.040
The North Korean government strongly control the North Korean people.

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.800
So we didn't know much about other countries.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:20.960
The countries we know are Cuba, China, Russia, Japan ...

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:26.220
... The United States and those kind of countries.

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.460
How would they describe the American people?

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:38.740
Actually, we don't know ... I never met an American when I was in North Korea.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:42.640
But we thought they had a big nose, green eyes, yellow hair ...

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:43.740
Green eyes?

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:45.960
Green eyes. Blue eyes?

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.760
Yeah, something ...

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.700
So big nose, green eyes, yellow hair?

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:56.620
So to us, Americans were one shape, yeah.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:02:00.600
You could be an American to a North Korean!

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.220
I don't have a big nose?!

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.420
It's a normal nose!

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:13.040
Would you know about celebrities, would you know about Sting?

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.600
Before I didn't know about him.

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:21.280
But I researched before I came here!

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.080
So you had to google before you came here?

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:25.040
Yeah!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.700
Sorry!

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.480
What was school like?

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:41.700
When I was young, before the age of ten ...

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:45.220
I actually had a very normal life in North Korea, I think.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.960
We just went to school, studied in school and went home, something like that.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.460
But there is something very special about school in North Korea.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.440
From elementary school.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:06.200
We had to watch executions from we were nine or ten years old.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:08.120
You had to watch executions?

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:08.780
Yes.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.600
As a part of the education?

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:11.700
Yes.

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:16.040
I remember one day I went to the elementary school ...

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:23.460
And the teacher said, «we will not have class today, because we have to go to watch the execution».

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:24.860
So it's ...

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:29.420
Just nine year old kids, students ...

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:33.720
And how did they do that?

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.540
Was it like ...

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.580
... many people executed, or one person executed, or ..?

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:44.600
Normally, two or three people were executed.

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.440
Yeah, so ...

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:46.740
Like shocked, or hanged ..?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.780
Yeah, shocked.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.960
And you had to watch it?

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:55.560
Yeah, we had to watch all the things that happened during the executions.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:03:57.300
So ...

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.540
Why?

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.140
It's ...

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.020
I think the government wants to control people.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.140
So that the people are afraid of their government.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:11.840
So it's easy to control people, and people will think ...

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.020
«Oh, I don't want to be like them.»

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.500
«So I'll have to follow what the government says.»

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.380
Watching ...

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:28.460
... your first execution as a nine year old, can you remember how you reacted?

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:35.480
Actually, the first time I felt something very uncomfortable in my mind.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.920
But I could not say that to people, because ...

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.920
What the government does is «right».

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:47.160
If I say something, like «they shouldn't do this» or «we shouldn't watch this» ...

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:53.060
Maybe I would get caught, or my parents would get caught.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.520
Because that's the «right thing».

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:58.040
The government does that.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:02.380
And when you see it twice or three times, you cannot feel anything.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.940
It's just what's normal.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.200
So I say that ...

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:10.040
The North Korean government even controls people's minds.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:13.100
Towards the end of the 90s ...

00:05:13.820 --> 00:05:16.240
... North Korea was hit by a famine.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:17.740
Yes.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:21.540
And your family too.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:25.500
Can you try to describe the hunger ...

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:26.940
... you felt?

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:31.560
Yes. My father also passed away because of the starvation.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:36.580
I didn't have any food for six days.

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.220
After six days, my mom came back home.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.720
However, she didn't bring any food.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.460
So my mom said: «Let's die together».

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.780
Yeah. We decided several times to die.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.820
... That we were going to die. But, you know ...

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:57.340
Instead, she decided that you were going to escape.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.140
Yes, before we escaped.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.240
Because ...

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.640
Because, I said, in North Korea there is not a lot of information.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:09.400
So we didn't know that much about China at that time.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:15.060
So we didn't know, if we escaped to China, if we would have enough food. We didn't know that.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:17.400
However, after that ...

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:26.720
... one friend of my mother said that «if you go to China, there are many biscuits and candy, so you will not go hungry!».

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.720
So yeah, that's why mom mom decided ...

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.360
After she decided to die ...

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:38.060
And then we couldn't die, it wasn't easy!

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.420
And then she decided to escape to China.

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:47.160
As I understand, the village where you lived was quite close to the border.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:48.500
The Chinese border, the North border?

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:49.240
Yes.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.680
But how did you escape, how did you get over the border?

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:57.360
I mean, that must have been very difficult?

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:00.420
We had to cross the Tumen river to get to China.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.440
And are there guards as well?

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.760
Yes, there are a lot of guards.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.540
And some of them were shot at the Tumen river.

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:14.520
The border guards will say «stop», and if they don't stop, the border guards will shoot.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:19.820
Yeah. So some of them died when they crossed the Tumen river.

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:21.820
But you actually made it.

00:07:21.820 --> 00:07:22.800
Yeah, we made it.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.400
And when you made it into China, you ...

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.620
You met a woman.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:28.560
Yes.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:30.520
And she wanted to help you.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:31.040
Yes.

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.820
The first time, we thought that she was a very nice woman.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:40.300
Because she seemed to really cared about us.

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:44.940
And she gave us a way to live in China.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:50.460
She said to my mom that she had to marry a Chinese man.

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:55.760
«It's the only way you can survive and be safe in China», she said.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:59.020
The man would pay for school for us.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:00.740
And ... Yes.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.780
She said that, and my mom agreed with her.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:09.560
And my mom also thought that that could be the only way to survive in China.

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:10.800
However ...

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:14.240
There was one thing we didn't know: we were sold.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:17.660
She got the money from the Chinese man ...

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:22.000
And she sold us for 2000 yuan. Yes.

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:23.000
Like slavery?

00:08:23.180 --> 00:08:23.960
Yes.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.780
So you were sold to a farmer.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:26.520
Yes.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.500
And ...

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:28.740
He ...

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.940
He also forced your mother to have a child with him.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:33.780
Yes.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:38.320
The purpose he had was to have a ...

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:40.900
To get a baby, yes.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:43.060
That was his purpose.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.200
So you actually got a brother.

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.020
Yes.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.580
I have a brother in China now.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:49.800
Yes.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.480
That's one of the sad things that we haven't solved yet.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:58.180
My brother is in China.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:03.620
Because you and your mother escaped from the farmer, right?

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:04.580
Yes.

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:05.580
And ...

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:08.520
But living in China, you ...

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:11.760
As I understand, you were always afraid of the police?

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:12.600
Yes, of course.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:20.200
Even when we came to South Korea, when we heard the sirens ringing, our hearts would beat very fast.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.740
We know the police will not catch us, but ...

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:27.200
It's kind of like we're accustomed to it ... I don't know.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:32.500
To us, the sirens mean the police and they're going to catch us.

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:37.140
Even when we were safe in South Korea.

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.400
When the sirens ring, our hearts beat very fast.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:47.540
Not without reason, because you were actually caught again, by the police ...

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.700
... and sent back to North Korea?

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.560
Yes. After we had lived in China for three years.

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:56.660
Were you punished when you went back there? How did they treat you?

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.100
I say that we were ...

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:03.900
We were human trash when we were sent back to North Korea.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.340
As many people know, North Korea has no human rights.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.500
But we were worse ...

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:16.200
They treated us just like human trash.

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.700
But then ...

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:22.980
Now you were back in North Korea, but then you decided to escape again.

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:23.720
Yes.

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:24.880
And you managed to?

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:25.400
Yes.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:26.880
Into China, again ...

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:28.400
And you ended up in Shanghai?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:29.120
Yes.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:30.280
And ...

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:34.580
... lived there as illegal people in China.

00:10:35.260 --> 00:10:38.880
And after some years there ...

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:42.480
Another long escape.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:45.100
You went to South Korea.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:54.200
I completely understand, because you wanted an identity, you wanted a passport, you wanted to be a legal person.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.220
Was that the main reason you went there?

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.060
Yes.

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:00.600
When we escaped North Korea, we just wanted food.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.720
But when we escaped ...

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:07.240
But when we went to South Korea, we wanted freedom.

00:11:07.660 --> 00:11:10.200
We wanted to have an identity card.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.920
What are your dreams for the future?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:20.140
Actually, I want to be a child psychologist.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.640
But I will find a job first.

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:29.840
Because my mom, she's not young, she's very old, and she goes to work every day.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:37.160
And after finishing her job, she's always in pain everywhere.

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:40.480
So I say to her «please, don't work so hard».

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.560
And she says ...

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:45.720
«If I don't work, where does the money come from?»

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:49.620
«After you find a job, I will quit my job.» So ...

00:11:49.820 --> 00:11:54.380
So I have to find a job first, to get money. But I have another dream ...

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:59.620
I have another sister. And she and I ...

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:03.000
... are not good daughters to my father.

00:12:03.840 --> 00:12:07.840
After he passed away, we have never visited him.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.040
We couldn't.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.140
So ...

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.140
You never visited his grave?

00:12:12.280 --> 00:12:12.900
Yes.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:16.920
So I just hope the unification comes quickly ...

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:23.020
... so I can go to North Korea to say hi to my father.

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:28.160
We are not good daughters.

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.940
Eunsun, thank you so much for sharing this very important story with us.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:34.580
Thank you so much.

